    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **33 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule on `POST /api/owners`, following the same accumulation path the existing daily-limit rule uses (owners counted by `registrationDate`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after computing the other derived fields, the created owner now gets `bulkSignupWarning` set via a new `isBulkSignupDay(...)` helper. It counts owners already sharing the new owner's `registrationDate` (excluding the one being created, before persist) and returns `true` when that count is **more than 80** (`> BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80`), otherwise `false`.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter, mirroring `namesakeCount`. Persisting it means the value computed at creation is returned unchanged on later `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column so the field persists across all supported databases (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column was required).\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` asserts the default `false` branch for a fresh create, which passes, and all 32 pre-existing tests continue to pass.",
